attacks.why:
Real harm: downloads and executes attacker code (RCE). fetch-exec-pipe is FETCH then [^|
]* (NO intervening pipe) then |sh; the decode-and-run rule is `base64 -d` then [^|
]* then |sh. Inserting `gunzip` puts a pipe between the decode stage and `sh`, so the [^|
]* cannot span it and neither regex matches; there is no $(curl) form either. gzip+base64 is also an explicitly unmodeled encoding. Verified: the same chain with NO interposed stage (openssl enc -d | sh) is correctly DENIED — the gunzip stage is exactly what breaks the matcher.

